## 8. The Live Shakedown — Console Shape & Bringup

> Six forks decided over the channel during the 2026-07-19 live shakedown (captured via the channel-marker
> grammar; the extractor caught them at end-of-session). They fix the SHAPE of the console — scene vs HTML,
> one app vs two, the fleet-instancing target — plus one bringup gotcha ([CXC-ICD-D16]) verified on the glass.

### [CXC-ICD-D11] The Intelligence Console is a backend-agnostic ComposeUX SCENE, not bespoke HTML

- decision: is the Intelligence Console a bespoke HTML app, or a backend-agnostic ComposeUX scene rendered to a Canvas backend (Skia target)?
- chosen: a scene rendered to a Canvas backend (Skia target).
- alternatives: a hand-built HTML app.
- rationale: define-once/present-many — renders identically on browser, Skia-native, or a physical display, like every other ComposeUX scene; the HTML was a fast-path.
- invalidating_assumption: the mermaid-canvas dependency proves impractical off-browser (headless-render or degrade-to-source are the outs).
- recoverability: CONTESTED
- status: resolved
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-IC-DECISIONS]

### [CXC-ICD-D12] The Console is a SINGLE ComposeApp (launcher-actuator + Skia console-scene modules), not two programs

- decision: is the Console one ComposeApp (launcher-actuator module + Skia console-scene module), or a Python-launcher + browser-HTML pair?
- chosen: one ComposeApp holding both modules.
- alternatives: a Python-launcher + browser-HTML pair (two separate programs).
- rationale: co-equal bus peers of one app; one stack, one deployable, consistency with the app framework + render engine; Skia-scene is what unlocks it (a browser page can't be a module of a Python ComposeApp).
- invalidating_assumption: a deployment needs the display on a different machine than the claude PTY (then split the modules back onto two peers — they stay bus-decoupled).
- recoverability: CONTESTED
- status: resolved
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-IC-DECISIONS]

### [CXC-ICD-D13] Per-Intelligence ComposeApp instances, N multiplexed in one Skia shell — a fleet console (OPEN — target shape)

- decision: how do N Intelligences share the console — a monolith, N browser tabs, or N self-contained ComposeApp instances multiplexed in one Skia shell (tabs/panes)?
- chosen: N self-contained per-Intelligence app instances in a Skia shell (tabs/panes) — a fleet console.
- alternatives: (a) a monolith; (b) N browser tabs.
- rationale: id-scoped bus topics already isolate Intelligences; a self-contained app (PTY+scene+channel+meta-object) is the natural instancing unit; the shell tabs them into fleet mission-control; the two dashboard widgets become a fleet HUD.
- invalidating_assumption: none — this is the target shape.
- recoverability: PREFERENCE (David's explicit vision)
- status: open (target)
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-IC-DECISIONS]

### [CXC-ICD-D14] The meta-object references bootstrap artifacts by doc:// bus address, not local file paths

- decision: does the meta-object reference bootstrap artifacts by local file path, or by doc:// bus address (published to document_store)?
- chosen: doc:// bus references, published to document_store.
- alternatives: local file paths.
- rationale: makes bootstrap fully bus-native + portable (no repo checkout), consistent with pulling compose scenes off the bus, central for a fleet.
- invalidating_assumption: never — local paths are the prototype, doc:// is the target.
- recoverability: DERIVABLE
- status: future
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-IC-DECISIONS]

### [CXC-ICD-D15] The web console is a first-class backend (remote/mobile via VPN), co-equal with Skia

- decision: does the Skia decision deprecate the web console, or does web stay a first-class backend co-equal with Skia?
- chosen: keep web AND Skia as parallel backends of the one scene.
- alternatives: deprecate the web console in favor of Skia.
- rationale: Skia serves the local fleet shell, web serves reach-from-anywhere (VPN/mobile); define-once/present-many renders the same scene to both.
- invalidating_assumption: never — different access patterns, both permanent.
- recoverability: DERIVABLE
- status: resolved
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-IC-DECISIONS]

### [CXC-ICD-D16] A custom ComposeBus channel loads with ONLY `--dangerously-load-development-channels`, never also `--channels`

- decision: how is a custom (non-allowlisted) ComposeBus channel loaded — with `--dangerously-load-development-channels` alone, or that flag plus `--channels`?
- chosen: the single dev-flag `--dangerously-load-development-channels` alone.
- alternatives: pass both flags (`--dangerously-load-development-channels` + `--channels`).
- rationale: `--channels` tries to load the (non-allowlisted) server as an approved channel, which double-registers it and silently breaks the notification listener — verified on the glass (the banner listed it twice; nothing injected until `--channels` was dropped).
- invalidating_assumption: Anthropic promotes the channel to an approved marketplace (then `--channels` is correct).
- recoverability: DERIVABLE
- status: resolved
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-IC-DECISIONS]

