**Status**: Living ledger, opened 2026-07-19. Records the twenty-two load-bearing forks of the Intelligence Console arc
([SPEC:CXC-INTELLIGENCE-CONSOLE], spec 34): transport = native channels over a composeio-native/Haven mine-bridge
split ([CXC-ICD-D1]/[CXC-ICD-D2]); lifecycle = launcher-as-actuator `/compact` + `--resume` for the initial move
([CXC-ICD-D3]/[CXC-ICD-D4]); the `channel` KIND proposal ([CXC-ICD-D5]); capture-the-pair corpus ([CXC-ICD-D6]);
the externalize-to-LTS principle this ledger applies to itself ([CXC-ICD-D7]); manifest-driven `self/registered`
([CXC-ICD-D8]); two hygiene/preference calls ([CXC-ICD-D9]/[CXC-ICD-D10]); the six live-shakedown console-shape
forks ([CXC-ICD-D11]..[CXC-ICD-D16]) — scene-not-HTML, one-app-not-two, the per-Intelligence fleet-console target,
doc:// bootstrap addressing, web-as-co-equal-backend, and the dev-channel load-flag gotcha verified on the glass;
and six more from the same day's console-design/safety session ([CXC-ICD-D17]..[CXC-ICD-D22]) — the work-flavor
visual blend (collaboration layout + instrument palette), the transcript→bus streams architecture and the
self-injection safety boundary it must hold (narration never rides the actuation channel, by construction), the
two-publisher avatar arbitration (explicit always wins over inferred), the harness monitor's perceive/act split
(statusline perceives, launcher acts), and the AUQ question widget's native-emit-over-channel-relay call.
Each fork carries an epistemic-recoverability tag so a successor knows the cold-start move: re-derive a DERIVABLE,
re-walk a CONTESTED, route a PREFERENCE back to the human. THREE remain LIVE — [CXC-ICD-D5] and [CXC-ICD-D10]
(OPEN, awaiting David) plus [CXC-ICD-D13] (the per-Intelligence fleet console, David's OPEN target shape, not yet
built); [CXC-ICD-D14] is resolved-but-FUTURE (doc:// is the target, local paths the prototype); [CXC-ICD-D19]
carries one OPEN follow-up ACTION, not a fork (authenticate the actuation channel — not yet built). This ledger is
the first application of [CXC-ICD-D7]: the rationale a `/compact` cannot carry, pinned in LTS.
